  "correction": {
    "one_sentence": "One holder's one mechanic on one subject is one debuff: a second trigger refreshes the window the first opened instead of arming a second modifier beside it.",
    "site": "src/calculator/survival/transitions.py::_apply_damage_modifier, through the new _refresh_live_modifier",
    "identity": "(source, armed_by), where armed_by is the roster slot that authored the packet — deliberately not `holder`, which is the owner skip's slot and is -1 for exactly the coupled-authoritative mechanics that need this most.",
    "surviving_window": "the later expiry (WindowMerge.EXTEND's reading, and the union interpreters.delta_amp.windows already performs pair-side), so a refresh never truncates a longer earlier window.",
    "not_touched": "Two different holders keep two modifiers. Whether they should is HolderStacking's question and D-66's ArmingLedger is the one place it is answered; this rule may not become a second answer to it, and tests/test_modifier_rearm.py pins that both directions.",
    "why_it_had_no_symptom": "_apply_cross_participant_modifiers writes support_damage_multiplier once per applying modifier, so the published receipt carried the LAST factor while the product was applied — a number the model computed that its own receipt contradicts."
  },
